# World of Warcraft Lore: A-Z (Vanilla WoW Only)

**A for Azeroth** — The world itself, home to both the Alliance and Horde.

**B for Blackrock Spire** — The mountain fortress of the Dark Iron dwarves and Black Dragonflight, home to Rend and Nefarian.

**C for Cenarius** — The demigod of the night elves, teacher of druidism, slain by Grom Hellscream.

**D for Durotar** — The harsh orc homeland in Kalimdor, named after Durotan of the Frostwolf clan.

**E for Elwynn Forest** — The lush human starting zone surrounding Stormwind.

**F for Felwood** — The corrupted forest in northern Kalimdor, tainted by the Burning Legion's presence.

**G for Gnomeregan** — The fallen gnome capital, irradiated after Sicco Thermaplugg's betrayal.

**H for Hyjal** — Mount Hyjal, site of the Third War's final battle and the World Tree Nordrassil.

**I for Ironforge** — The great dwarven capital carved into the mountain of Dun Morogh.

**J for Jintha'Alor** — The troll city in the Hinterlands, seat of the Vilebranch tribe.

**K for Karazhan** — The mysterious tower of Medivh in Deadwind Pass (though not yet a raid in vanilla).

**L for Lordaeron** — The fallen human kingdom, its capital now Undercity beneath the ruins.

**M for Molten Core** — The fiery raid beneath Blackrock Mountain, domain of Ragnaros the Firelord.

**N for Naxxramas** — The necropolis citadel of the Scourge, floating above Stratholme.

**O for Orgrimmar** — The Horde's capital in Durotar, named for Orgrim Doomhammer.

**P for Plaguelands** — The Eastern and Western Plaguelands, ravaged by the Scourge's plague.

**Q for Quel'Thalas** — The ancient homeland of the high elves (referenced in vanilla lore).

**R for Ragnaros** — The Firelord himself, summoned by the Dark Iron dwarves and bound to Molten Core.

**S for Stormwind** — The human capital, rebuilt after the Second War.

**T for Teldrassil** — The new World Tree, home of the night elves and their capital Darnassus.

**U for Un'Goro Crater** — The primordial jungle teeming with dinosaurs and elementals.

**V for Vashj** — Lady Vashj, the naga leader (appearing in vanilla lore as a major figure).

**W for Winterspring** — The snowy region of northern Kalimdor, home to the furbolgs and Wintersaber trainers.

**X for Xavian** — The satyr-infested ruins in Ashenvale.

**Y for Yojamba Isle** — The Zandalar troll outpost off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.

**Z for Zul'Gurub** — The troll raid in Stranglethorn Vale, where Hakkar the Soulflayer awaits.

How'd I do? Any spots you'd have chosen differently? [end of text]


